   The constructed class identity is grounded by Z_Construct_UClass_ULuxParticleSystemComponent,
   exact class size 0xAD0, all five callers, component fields, template setup, registration, and
   activation.
   
   Source
   SoulcaliburVI.exe 0x140898490.
   
   Audit correction (2026-09-09)
   The legacy field label dwAutoActivateFlags is misleading: +0x8B8 bit0 is the completion
   auto-destruction selector. Construction alone does not perform the caller's world registration,
   activation, completion-delegate binding or manager-slot publication. Native emitter
   initialization 141F7A6D0 can call rand; rematerialization therefore requires complete B undo
   before any native publication/initialization, and explicit accounting for new component,
   scheduler, emitter, pool and render ownership. No pending-kill flag revival is implied. */

UParticleSystemComponent_TemplateState_Partial *
InitializeParticleSystemComponentFromTemplate
          (UParticleSystem_TemplateMetadata_Partial *pParticleTemplate,
          UObject_Partial *pDefaultOuter,UObject_Partial *pOverrideOuter,bool bAutoDestroy)

{
